---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Soha Sami">
  <section class="inner-hero shell" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow">About Soha</p>
    <h1>Economics.<br />Mathematics.<br /><em>Energy.</em></h1>
  </section>

  <section class="about-intro shell" data-reveal>
    <div class="about-intro-label">
      <span>01</span>
      <p>Background</p>
    </div>

    <div class="about-intro-copy">
      <p class="about-lead">
        I am a graduate student working across energy markets, quantitative
        finance and climate-related risk.
      </p>

      <p>
        My academic background combines economics and mathematics with graduate
        training in energy market finance and financial mathematics. I started
        with Economics and Mathematics at the University of Delhi and am now
        completing graduate studies in Europe through the Erasmus Mundus
        GrEnFin programme alongside Financial and Insurance Mathematics at
        LMU Munich.
      </p>

      <p>
        My studies have taken me between Bologna, Paris and Munich, with each
        programme adding a different part of the quantitative and economic
        toolkit I use in my work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="education-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <span class="section-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Education</p>
          <h2>Three degrees.<br /><em>One direction.</em></h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="education-list">

        <article class="education-item" data-reveal>
          <div class="education-year">2025–2027</div>

          <div class="education-content">
            <p class="education-type">CURRENT · GRADUATE STUDIES</p>
            <h3>Erasmus Mundus GrEnFin</h3>
            <h4>Greening Energy Market and Finance</h4>

            <p>
              A joint European master's programme focused on the economics,
              finance and transformation of energy markets. My studies cover
              electricity markets, energy finance, climate and business,
              quantitative methods and the changing structure of European
              energy systems.
            </p>

            <div class="education-universities">
              <span>Università di Bologna</span>
              <span>Université Paris Dauphine-PSL</span>
              <span>LMU Munich</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="education-item" data-reveal>
          <div class="education-year">2025–2027</div>

          <div class="education-content">
            <p class="education-type">GRADUATE STUDIES · MUNICH</p>
            <h3>MSc Financial and Insurance Mathematics</h3>
            <h4>Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München</h4>

            <p>
              My quantitative training at LMU focuses on the mathematical
              foundations of finance and risk. I am developing skills in
              stochastic modelling, quantitative risk management, financial
              mathematics, numerical methods and statistical modelling.
            </p>

            <div class="education-tags">
              <span>Stochastic Modelling</span>
              <span>Quantitative Risk</span>
              <span>Financial Mathematics</span>
              <span>Numerical Methods</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="education-item" data-reveal>
          <div class="education-year">2021–2025</div>

          <div class="education-content">
            <p class="education-type">FOUNDATION · NEW DELHI</p>
            <h3>BA Economics & Mathematics</h3>
            <h4>University of Delhi</h4>

            <p>
              My bachelor's degree gave me the foundation that connects the
              economic and quantitative sides of my work. Studying economics
              alongside mathematics developed my understanding of economic
              systems, statistical analysis, mathematical methods and
              quantitative reasoning.
            </p>

            <div class="education-tags">
              <span>Economics</span>
              <span>Mathematics</span>
              <span>Statistics</span>
              <span>Quantitative Analysis</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="journey-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <span class="section-number">03</span>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Academic journey</p>
          <h2>New Delhi →<br />Bologna → Paris → <em>Munich</em></h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="journey-grid">

        <div class="journey-place" data-reveal>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>New Delhi</h3>
          <p>Economics & Mathematics</p>
          <small>2021–2025</small>
        </div>

        <div class="journey-place" data-reveal>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Bologna</h3>
          <p>Energy markets & finance</p>
          <small>GrEnFin</small>
        </div>

        <div class="journey-place" data-reveal>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Paris</h3>
          <p>Climate & Business</p>
          <small>Paris Dauphine-PSL</small>
        </div>

        <div class="journey-place active" data-reveal>
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Munich</h3>
          <p>Financial & Insurance Mathematics</p>
          <small>LMU Munich</small>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-focus-section">
    <div class="shell about-focus-grid">

      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">What I am learning</p>
        <h2>Building the<br /><em>toolkit.</em></h2>
      </div>

      <div class="focus-columns" data-reveal>

        <div>
          <span>ENERGY</span>
          <p>Electricity markets</p>
          <p>Market design</p>
          <p>Renewable generation</p>
          <p>Flexibility</p>
          <p>Power price dynamics</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>QUANTITATIVE</span>
          <p>Stochastic modelling</p>
          <p>Quantitative risk management</p>
          <p>Numerical methods</p>
          <p>Monte Carlo simulation</p>
          <p>Dependence modelling</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>COMPUTATIONAL</span>
          <p>Python</p>
          <p>Statistical analysis</p>
          <p>Data pipelines</p>
          <p>Git & GitHub</p>
          <p>Reproducible research</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="scholarship-section">
    <div class="shell scholarship-grid" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Erasmus Mundus</p>
        <h2>Studying across<br /><em>Europe.</em></h2>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p class="scholarship-title">
          Erasmus Mundus Joint Master in Greening Energy Market and Finance
        </p>
        <p>
          The scholarship has allowed me to study energy markets and finance
          across different European academic environments, combining the
          economic perspective of energy transition with quantitative and
          financial training.
        </p>
        <p>
          The mobility is an important part of the programme: rather than
          studying the energy transition from one academic system, I have
          experienced different approaches across Italy, France and Germany.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-end shell" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow">Currently</p>
    <h2>Energy markets, quantitative finance,<br /><em>and what connects them.</em></h2>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
